## 1. Fault confirmed on the VISUAL path (extends doc C)
Abort is NOT collision-specific, as compute-mesh-aabb.py's docstring implied.
Backtrace (GDB, LD_LIBRARY_PATH cleared for the inferior):

  terminate called after throwing an instance of 'std::logic_error'
    what():  basic_string: construction from null is not valid

  gz::sim::v10::RenderUtil::Update()
    -> SceneManager::CreateVisual()
    -> SceneManager::LoadGeometry()
    -> gz::sim::v10::loadMesh()
    -> gz::common::MeshManager::Load()
    -> gz::common::ColladaLoader::Load()
    -> ColladaLoader::Implementation::LoadGeometry()   <-- throws

Cause: SketchUp edge geometry in the .dae exports, as Collada <lines>.
The throw happens in a Qt event handler, so the GUI cannot catch it.

## 2. Evidence that <lines> is the cause
Isolated test (separate partition ao_meshtest_iso3, own container, /t bind
mount, stripped copies only) vs production:
  - original meshes -> aborts ~1s after "Camera pose topic advertised"
  - <lines> stripped -> GUI stays up, renders, zero "Failed to load mesh"
NOTE: an earlier run of this test was INVALID — the GUI container lacked the
/t mount, so meshes were simply absent and "no abort" proved nothing.
The test was redone with the mount present and only the mesh content changed.

## 3. Fix applied
New tool: scripts/simulation/strip-collada-lines.py
  - removes <lines>...</lines> and <lines .../> only
  - refuses to write if no <triangles> survives (guards a bad regex)
  - never edits a source export in place
Blocks removed / bytes:
  09-SIMULATIONARMS.dae                     36 blocks  -6248
  09-SIMULATIONCONVEYOR.dae                220 blocks -59407
  09-SIMULATIONMASSING-ADUDOORS_FABRICATIONAREA.dae
                                          107 blocks -86417
  09-SIMULATIONVEHICLES-ARMS.dae           610 blocks -244203
Output written to GAZEBO/models/factory_assets/meshes/*.dae, replacing four
SYMLINKS. The massing_fab symlink was already BROKEN (embedded newline in the
target path). Original SketchUp exports in /ALWAYSON/GAZEBO are untouched.
All four verified: 0 <lines>, <triangles> intact (462/140/196/572), XML parses.

