## 5. Main-monitor placement — three things that did NOT work
Main monitor measured: DP-3, priority 1, geometry 0,738 1920x1080.
DP-1 is portrait, 1920,0 1080x1920. xrandr --listmonitors confirms.

  a) kwinrc [Window Rules][100] with geometry=0,738,1920,1080
     -> reconfigure returned 0, no warning, and NOTHING happened.
        Window still mapped at 1200x1000+1800+474. Rule removed.
  b) KWin script using workspace.windowAdded / workspace.windowScreenChanged
     -> windowScreenChanged does NOT exist in 6.6.6; "Cannot call method
        'connect' of undefined". Verified by dumping Object.keys(workspace).
     -> workspace.outputs() does NOT exist either; the list is
        workspace.screens, entries have .name and .geometry.
     -> metadata.json needed "KPackageStructure": "KWin/Script".
  c) Script matching client.resourceClass === "gz-sim-gui"
     -> silently matched nothing. The live value is "Gazebo GUI";
        client.resourceName is "gz-sim-gui". Matching must use resourceName.

  Working script: ~/.local/share/kwin/scripts/ao-gazebo-monitor/
    contents.js + metadata.json (loaded via /Scripting, start()).
  Confirmed:  js: ao-gazebo-monitor: placed gz-sim-gui on DP-3 1920x1080+0+738
  xwininfo:  "Gazebo Sim" 1920x1052+0+766   (was +1800+474)
  (+766 vs +738 is the window frame/title bar; width 1052 vs 1080 likewise.)

  NOTE: the script is loaded at runtime. It is NOT yet wired to autostart,
